A||N||6||Daleford||Hedders for a 4.9||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-15-2000||09:24 AM||||WIth the popularity of the 4.9 V-8 in the Fiero, is there any word on hedders becoming available for this swap?||||reg||5
Z||000001||HarryG||12-15-2000||12:01 PM||||Right now, you're on your own for headers. I don't think anyone even has a flange kit available if you wanted to build a set. Not a small job, but if you're a good welder or have a buddy that is, it could be done. Making improvements to the exhaust system is one of the few things (other than adding nitrous)which an owner presently could do to upgrade the 4.9. I've looked around, and the performance parts situation is dismal. Found a cam company offering reground cams for the earlier 4.1-4.5's, but I don't know if these could be made to work in a 4.9.  <P>FYI: if you decide to build headers, look at <A HREF="http://www.headersbyed.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.headersbyed.com/</A>   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||12-15-2000||02:49 PM||||"All" it would take would be an appropriate manifold base to use a TPI on a 4.9. I'll get right on it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||12-15-2000||04:21 PM||||The 4.9 uses cast iron exhaust manifolds. I think the tube style manifolds from a 4.1 will fit. I haven't measured port sizes yet, I don't know if they flow any better or worse. I'd like to use them just for weight reduction. I'm not sure the 4.9 would benefit from larger headers, they look plenty big. Just use a high flow cat and muffler. Also, the rearward outlet can be capped, and either a dual exhaust or a custom Y-pipe can be used in place of the factory crossover pipe.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||12-15-2000||07:26 PM||||would it be worth having the stock manifolds extrude honed?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Daleford||12-15-2000||10:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>"All" it would take would be an appropriate manifold base to use a TPI on a 4.9. I'll get right on it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Will. We have led you astray.... we are talking about EXHAUST manifolds. <BR>thanks anyway<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||12-15-2000||11:34 PM||||I know you're talking about exhaust manifolds. Those are easier to make than a good intake system.<BR>     How good is the 4.9 intake manifold? From the pictures I've seen, it looks like it's been squashed down for hood clearance. I wouldn't think something like that would have the greatest flow characteristics...||||reg||1
